av-grade quartz accelerometer?","u":"Quantum preset: a cold-atom interferometer (CAI) accelerometer, built from its interferometer physics, against a navigation-grade quartz accelerometer during a GNSS outage.","b":"The cold-atom-interferometer stays within 100 m for 1 h 50 min; the nav-grade-quartz for 6 min.","l":"Holdover is how long each navigator stays inside the 100 m budget after satellite navigation is lost.","f":[["Holdover, cold-atom-interferometer","1 h 50 min","","inside 100 m",1,0],["Holdover, nav-grade-quartz","6 min","","inside 100 m",0,0],["Error, 95 % of the time, cold-atom-interferometer","9.855","m","over the whole run",0,0],["Error, 95 % of the time, nav-grade-quartz","30640","m","over the whole run",0,0]]},"hybrid-optical-rf":{"k":"Inertial & alternative navigation · Optical/RF hybrid","c":"var(--nav)","t":"What continuity and integrity does combining optical and RF (radio frequency) PNT (positioning, navigation and timing) buy?","u":"Heterogeneous optical + RF PNT joint availability / precision / integrity (P5).","b":"Combining optical and radio ranging gives protection levels of 6.248 m horizontal and 6.626 m vertical.","l":"The consistency test reads 0 against a threshold of 28.47: no fault is flagged.","f":[["Chi2 statistic","0","","",0,0],["Chi2 threshold","28.47","","",0,0],["HPL","6.248","m","",0,0],["N axes","4","","",0,0]]},"fusion-pnt-coupled":{"k":"Inertial & alternative navigation · Coupled sensor-fusion navigator","c":"var(--nav)","t":"With one stacked Kalman filter over position, clock and accelerometer bias, how does the navigator ride out a GNSS (global navigation satellite system) outage?","u":"Coupled joint sensor-fusion PNT (positioning, navigation and timing): the same suites and GNSS outage as `fusion-pnt.toml`, but the navigator is ONE stacked Kalman filter over position, velocity, clock phase, clock frequency and the accelerometer bias (the `[coupled]` table).","b":"The quantum suite holds position and time for 1 h 50 min;