+<!-- seo:body --><noscript><section class="crawl-text"><h1>Kshana Studio</h1><p>Kshana Studio runs Kshana, the open-source PNT (positioning, navigation and timing) resilience simulator, in your browser: the engine runs locally as WebAssembly, so nothing is installed and nothing is uploaded. Pick a GNSS (global navigation satellite system) jamming, spoofing, clock holdover, integrity or lunar navigation scenario, tune it, replay it, compare runs, sweep a parameter and download a reproducible report. It needs JavaScript.</p><h2>Scenarios it runs (185)</h2><ul><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=acm-link&amp;tab=overview">acm-link</a>: DVB-S2 adaptive coding and modulation (ACM) along one satellite&#x27;s passes over one station.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aocs-slew&amp;tab=overview">aocs-slew</a>: Reaction-wheel attitude slew under MRP feedback, closed on the true state.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aocs-slew-mekf&amp;tab=overview">aocs-slew-mekf</a>: Reaction-wheel attitude slew under MRP feedback, closed on an MEKF estimate.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=aperture-duty-cycle&amp;tab=overview">aperture-duty-cycle</a>: Aperture duty-cycle demonstrator (ground segment &amp; operations).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=araim-gps-galileo&amp;tab=timeseries">araim-gps-galileo</a>: Dual-constellation ARAIM availability: GPS + Galileo evaluated with the advanced</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=araim-reference-check&amp;tab=overview">araim-reference-check</a>: The engine&#x27;s ARAIM protection levels against the WG-C subgroup&#x27;s OWN worked examples.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=ascent-losses&amp;tab=overview">ascent-losses</a>: Gravity-turn ascent losses of an ILLUSTRATIVE two-stage kerosene/oxygen launcher (no real</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=attitude-budget&amp;tab=overview">attitude-budget</a>: 3-DOF attitude &amp; pointing error budget demonstrator (pre-hardware AOCS/GNC).</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=automotive-urban-canyon&amp;tab=holdover">automotive-urban-canyon</a>: Road vehicle through an urban canyon: GNSS/INS dead-reckoning across an underpass and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-jam-spoof-holdover-integrity&amp;tab=campaign&amp;play=1">campaign-jam-spoof-holdover-integrity</a>: A chained mission: nominal, jamming, spoofing, GNSS loss with clock holdover and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-monte-carlo-clock-holdover&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-monte-carlo-clock-holdover</a>: A seeded Monte Carlo ensemble through a campaign, on a case with a closed form.</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-optimize-link-budget&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-optimize-link-budget</a>: An optimisation through a campaign: the link-budget example&#x27;s X-band link</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-shared-jammer-sea-road&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-shared-jammer-sea-road</a>: Cross-domain composition: one jammer, two platforms. A ship in the Gulf of Finland</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-spectrum-holdover-integrity&amp;tab=campaign&amp;play=1">campaign-spectrum-holdover-integrity</a>: A chained mission driven by the L-band spectrum: a chirp jammer takes GPS L1 C/A and</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=campaign-sweep-jammer-power&amp;tab=campaign">campaign-sweep-jammer-power</a>: A parameter sweep through a campaign: the jamming example&#x27;s receiver (52 N, 4 E,</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-classical-pilot-signals&amp;tab=leo-signal">celeste-iod-classical-pilot-signals</a>: Celeste IOD signal designs: the frequency bands and the &quot;Classical Pilot&quot; signal</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-end-to-end&amp;tab=leo-chain">celeste-iod-end-to-end</a>: Celeste IOD end to end (optional preset): the E5 configuration #1 signal -&gt; a Celeste IOD</li><li><a href="/studio/?scenario=celeste-iod-fused-pvt&amp;tab=leo-positioning">celeste-iod-fused-pvt</a>: GNSS positioning joined by the two ESA Celeste in-orbit demonstration sat